```

This is a standard kernel function that safely copies data from user space to kernel space. It won't cause a buffer overflow because it's designed to handle this correctly.

```c
if (ret) {
    spin_lock_irqsave(&priv->spinlock, flags);
    buffer->next = priv->free;
