    }

    *local++ = p++;
}
```

This loop initializes local variables. It checks if a value is valid before using it, and sets it to undefined if not.

I don't see any obvious security vulnerabilities in this code. It seems to be properly handling memory layout and copying values between frames with bounds checking.

